{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--couplets-no-strict-formal-rules","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--couplet-structure"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu oral literature, couplets are not subject to strict rules or constraints, and rhyming or formal matching across lines is not a requirement.","ja":"アイヌ語の口承文芸において対句の作成には規則や制約がなく、行間で韻を踏んだり完全に一致させたりすることは対句の要件ではない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:endo2022@handbook-epub/l0066-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--poyyaunpe-toyyaunpe-pun-couplet","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--couplet-structure"],"statement":{"en":"In Horobetsu epics, the couplet 'Poyyaunpe / Toyyaunpe' using toy is sometimes used when enemy characters insult the hero, forming a pun between poy (< pon 'young') and toy.","ja":"幌別方言の叙事詩では、敵側の人物が主人公 Poyyaunpe を罵倒する際に toy を用いた Poyyaunpe / Toyyaunpe という対句を使うことがあり、poy（< pon「若い」）と toy で掛詞をなす。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":["enemy characters insulting the hero"]},"forms":["Poyyaunpe","Toyyaunpe","poy","toy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0590-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--wen-toy-couplet-intensification","differs_in":"scope","note":"Both involve toy but in different couplet functions: pun vs. intensification of badness"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--parallelism-reversible-line-order","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Parallelism in Ainu oral literature consists of a pair of lines with identical formal structure in which only specific words are substituted, and the order of the two lines is usually reversible.","ja":"対句とは、形式的には同一で一部の単語だけを入れ替えた2句一組の表現であり、その多くは前後の順序を入れ替えても同様に用いることができる。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0589-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--couplets-used-in-prose-too","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Parallelism (couplets) is not exclusively a technique of verse but is also frequently used within prose narratives, and therefore some couplets do not conform to the principles of poetic meter.","ja":"対句は必ずしも韻文の技法というわけではなく、散文説話などの中でも多用され、音律の原則には合わない対句もある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0591-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-couplet-expresses-many","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-formula"],"statement":{"en":"Couplets combining tu 'two' and re 'three' are frequently used to express the meaning 'many'.","ja":"tu「2つの」re「3つの」を組み合わせた対句表現が「たくさんの」という意味を表すために頻繁に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["tu","re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0591-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-couplet-two-structural-patterns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-formula"],"statement":{"en":"Couplets with tu and re have two structural patterns: 'tu + Noun + Verb, re + Noun + Verb' and 'tu + Noun, re + Noun, Verb'.","ja":"tu と re による対句には、「tu + 名詞 + 動詞 re + 名詞 + 動詞」という型と、「tu + 名詞 re + 名詞 動詞」という型がある。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["tu","re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0591-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--otu-ore-elevated-poetic-pattern","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-formula"],"statement":{"en":"As an even more elevated or poetic expression not used in daily conversation, the pattern otu ~ ore ~ is also used.","ja":"日常会話では使われないさらに雅語的なものとして、otu 〜 ore 〜 という表現も使われる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":["poetic/elevated register","not in daily conversation"]},"forms":["otu","ore"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0592-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-couplet-expresses-many","differs_in":"register","note":"otu/ore is the elevated/poetic register counterpart of the tu/re couplet"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-wan-re-wan-couplet","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-formula"],"statement":{"en":"With wan 'ten' added, the couplet tu wan ~ re wan ~ is also used.","ja":"wan「10の」を加えて、tu wan 〜 re wan 〜 という対句も使われる。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["wan","tu wan","re wan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0592-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-couplet-expresses-many","differs_in":"scope","note":"tu wan / re wan is an extended variant of the basic tu/re couplet"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-alone-expresses-many","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-formula"],"statement":{"en":"Because combining tu and re repeats the same expression, tu ~ alone can also express 'many'.","ja":"tu と re の組み合わせは同じ表現を重ねることになるため、tu 〜 だけで「たくさん」を表す場合もある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["tu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0592-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--tu-re-couplet-expresses-many","differs_in":"scope","note":"tu alone as a reduced form of the tu/re couplet for expressing 'many'"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--sirka-nuye-tomika-nuye-pan-dialectal","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--word-pairs"],"statement":{"en":"The synonymous parallel couplet sirka nuye / tomika nuye ('carving the scabbard / carving the treasured scabbard') is widely used across dialects to depict peaceful everyday life with a man engaged in carving by the hearth.","ja":"同義的対句 sirka nuye / tomika nuye（刀の鞘を彫り / 宝刀の鞘を彫り）は、男性が炉端で彫刻にいそしむ平穏な日常を表す表現として広く各方言で用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sirka nuye","tomika nuye"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0589-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--wen-toy-couplet-intensification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--word-pairs"],"statement":{"en":"The parallel couplet pattern 'wen ~ toy ~' is used to emphasize that something is terribly bad or that the degree of something is extreme.","ja":"wen ～ toy ～ という対句形式は、ひどく悪いことや程度がはなはだしいことを強調して表現する場合に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["wen","toy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0590-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--wen-toy-order-reversible","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--word-pairs"],"statement":{"en":"In the couplet 'wen ~ toy ~', the order of wen and toy may be either way.","ja":"wen ～ toy ～ の対句において、wen と toy の順番はどちらが先でもよい。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["wen","toy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0590-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--parallelism-reversible-line-order","differs_in":null,"note":"wen/toy reversibility is a specific instance of the general reversibility of couplet lines"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--rerko-long-time-couplet","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topics":["topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs","topic:register/parallelism-couplets-and-word-pairs--word-pairs"],"statement":{"en":"rerko, meaning 'three days' in the phrase tutko rerko 'two or three days', is also used to form a couplet expressing 'a long time' (e.g. kunne rerko / tokap rerko).","ja":"tutko rerko「2日、3日」で「3日」を表す rerko を用いて、「長い間」を表す対句（例：kunne rerko / tokap rerko）を作ることもある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["rerko","tutko rerko","kunne rerko","tokap rerko"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0592-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
